## SQ-CSI-01 | Curios hands, face, feet slots by IMC (bot at 140)
@group A
@commands Boot; join a bot or player; `/curios list`
@pass `hands`, `face`, `feet` listed alongside head, back, etc.; no IMC error naming creativeengineering in `logs/latest.log`
@fails listener not added (`CreativeEquipment` curios branch, `compat/CuriosSlots`) or jar stale
@from batches/r1102b/s3_A.qb
@reviewed 2026-11-20
# r1120lr batch fault: Curios 1.19.2's /curios list takes no player ('Incorrect argument'); the slot types come from /curios list, the bot's own slots from its ForgeCaps
bootreject (?i)IMC.*creative(equipment|compat|engineering).*(error|exception)
> forceload add 136 496 144 508
> pbot spawn csi 140 -60 503 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 2
> curios list
> data get entity csi ForgeCaps."curios:inventory".Curios
expect \bhands\b
expect \bface\b
expect \bfeet\b
expect has the following entity data: .*Identifier: "hands"
reject Incorrect argument for command|Unknown or incomplete command|No entity was found
look rows/SQ-CSI-01.log: the three new slots listed alongside head, back and the rest; the bot's ForgeCaps list hands, face and feet

## SQ-CSI-02
@group A
@commands `/curios list <bot>` on a bot that joined an existing world
@pass the bot has 1 slot each of hands, face, feet
@fails existing saves not getting new IMC slots (then note in curios_slots.md)
@reviewed 2026-11-20
@boot 2
# run on a later boot of the SQ-CSI-01 world (@boot 2: SQ-CSI-01 runs on boot 1 as setup): bot csi rejoins with its saved player data
# r1120lr batch fault: '/curios list csi' (no player argument in Curios 1.19.2) and the same boot as SQ-CSI-01; the bot's slots are read from its ForgeCaps
> forceload add 136 496 144 508
> pbot remove csi
> pbot spawn csi 140 -60 503 minecraft:overworld survival
> cdevtest tickwarp 40
waitlog verb=tickwarp end=done ticks=40 60
> data get entity csi ForgeCaps."curios:inventory".Curios
expect has the following entity data: .*Identifier: "hands"
expect has the following entity data: .*Identifier: "face"
expect has the following entity data: .*Identifier: "feet"
reject Incorrect argument for command|Unknown or incomplete command|No entity was found
look the world had SQ-CSI-01's bot csi saved on an earlier boot (else this is a first join and proves nothing): one slot each of hands, face, feet
